                <pb facs="0494" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg480"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>In a letter of January 5, 1948, Secretary of Defense Forrestal informed Secretary
                    of State Marshall that on December 31, 1947, the Secretaries of the Army, the
                    Navy, and the Air Force established the Joint United States Military Advisory
                    and Planning Group (Greece) in accordance with recommendations by the Joint
                    Chiefs of Staff. He noted that on the same day the Joint Chiefs of Staff
                    designated Major General William G. Livesay as Director of JUSMAPG. (868.20
                    Mission/1–548) Secretary Forrestal was replying to Secretary Marshall’s letter
                    of November 7, 1947, not printed, but see footnote 4, <ref target="#pg393">page
                        393</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
